From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:35:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): retain drain custody for K01 mutation children
 [daveey]

The offline helper introduced two unregistered subprocess seams, making the
whole-tree worker-drain ratchet fail unrelated required core CI. Route Git
listing and bounded Vitest runs through one popen_worker launcher, with a
scrubbed environment and inherited close-only lease retained by real children.
Kill/reap the direct child on timeout/interruption. Keep descendant descriptors
visible to the existing drain rather than claiming parent lifetime is custody.
Move script execution under main so behavior can be tested without a K01 run.
Inventory the single routed spawn honestly; preserve mutation definitions.

Proof:
- Baseline source-scan RED: 8 pass, 1 fail (only k01-mutants.py missing).
- Source-scan / text encoding / env consumers GREEN: 1728 pass.
- Real child/refusal/timeout/spawn-error/unactivated coverage plus fence and
  hardening consumers GREEN: 34 pass.
- Replacing popen_worker with raw Popen kills both draining/sealed tests
  (2 behavioral failures); restored helper file GREEN: 7 pass.
- Full canonical scripts/check: 21 checks pass, health 0 blocking/advisory.
  Used the pinned test interpreter; runtime bootstrap under isolated fake HOME
  is not a committed dependency environment on this worker profile.

Source/CI only. No native K01 execution, contained-runner release, restart,
installation or social action is authorized or performed.


